Revision history for JS::Minifier

{{$NEXT}}

    - Comments inside a template-literal ${...} expression (block or line,
      multi-line) are now consumed properly instead of being misread as the
      start of a regular expression literal (was: "unterminated regular
      expression literal" crash on valid input)
    - drop_console / drop_debugger now also remove statements terminated by
      an ASI line break (e.g. "debugger" or "console.log(x)" on their own
      line), while refusing to drop a console call that continues across the
      line break (e.g. before a '(' or binary operator, which would change
      semantics)
    - Initial release: a fork of JS::Minify by Sam Morrison, rewritten for
      performance and reliability
    - New CLI tool bin/jsminify
    - Shebang, bang-comment, template literal, and NOCOMPRESS support
    - drop_console/drop_debugger options; true/false shortened in value
      contexts; semicolons removed before closing braces
    - Numerous bug fixes (out-of-bounds reads, line continuation,
      unterminated string detection, division/regex misclassification,
      CRLF normalization, U+2028/U+2029 line terminators)